  - The front-door allow-list is the /24 plus ccs_internal_gw.
  - The keepalive is sent by WireGuard clients; OpenVPN clients do not send it (<design doc §>).
  - No project hard rule or earlier ballot fixes this value.
  a) allow 10.77.1.128/25, deny all
     - admits WireGuard clients; rejects OpenVPN clients and every other source
     - derived value; correct only while Pritunl's WG network is exactly that /25
     - cost if wrong: keepalives rejected, WG tunnels rebuild again;
       rollback: one-value change, one gateway run
  b) allow 10.77.1.0/24, deny all
     - admits WireGuard and OpenVPN clients; rejects every other source
     - the same value the front door uses; holds however the /24 is split
     - cost if wrong: OpenVPN clients can reach a path they do not use;
